Before you build the CQL rules, check whether your Linux sensors actually send UserLogon / UserLogonFailed2 with RemoteAddressIP4 filled in. Run #event_simpleName=UserLogonFailed2 event_platform=Lin | head(10) to see. If those fields are empty, SSH-06 to SSH-08 need /var/log/secure or auth.log ingested into NG-SIEM through a log collector, and the queries would need to be adapted to that log format.
For references, CrowdStrike documents the Custom IOA rule and rule-group APIs if you want to deploy these as code (CrowdStrike Developer Center), and the community repo blueteam-ioa-rules has export/import scripts.
